    "message": "Symbian: connect Belle native input, downloads and platform notifications\n\nAdd bounded response-to-download handoff, exclusive temporary files and native\nSave/Cancel UI without repeating POST. Keep unknown decoded lengths unknown,\ncoalesce final progress with a timer, refuse existing targets, and restore the\nattached native shell after modal Save. Avoid using a destroyed container.\n\nConnect native touch/pointer input, precise scrolling, trusted clipboard menu\nand keyboard operations, actual editable-hit FEP gating, HTTP 401 UI, native\nmonotonic time, memory pressure and connection-state adapters. Export EKA\nmodifier/FEP-cancel and SDK ECom/FEP build repairs with provenance.\n\nC19 engine build and browser link pass. Retain image-bound browser evidence for\nsix ordinary download cases plus transfer cancellation, seven touch sequences,\nnine keyboard and nine menu clipboard cases, five FEP cases and native timers.\nManager 38 checks, deferred queue 90, clipboard admission 24 and auth/network\nhost contracts pass. CI 0.3.42 artifact verification is archived separately.\n\nHTTP auth device matrix remains pending. Memory-pressure and online whole-run\nfailures remain FAIL with raw evidence; multi-touch and physical Belle need\nacceptance. CookieStore/IPv6/H2/IAP candidates are not included in this change.",
